+# OpenClaw
+
+## Overview
+
+OpenClaw is a multi-channel AI gateway with extensible messaging integrations. It allows you to connect AI models (OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, etc.) with various messaging platforms (Telegram, Discord, Slack, iMessage, Matrix, etc.).
+
+## Architecture
+
+- **Backend**: TypeScript/Node.js gateway server (`src/`) — handles AI model routing, channel integrations, webhooks, and automation
+- **Frontend UI**: Lit-based web control dashboard (`ui/`) — provides a management interface for the gateway
+- **Extensions**: Channel-specific plugins (`extensions/`) — e.g., Discord, Telegram, Slack, Matrix, etc.
+- **Packages**: Shared packages (`packages/`) — clawdbot, moltbot
+
+## Tech Stack
+
+- **Runtime**: Node.js 22+
+- **Package manager**: pnpm 10.26.1
+- **Frontend**: Lit (Web Components), Vite 7
+- **Backend**: TypeScript, Hono (web framework)
+- **Build**: tsdown (TypeScript bundler)
+
+## Development Workflow
+
+The `Start application` workflow runs the UI dev server:
+```
+cd ui && COREPACK_ENABLE_STRICT=0 pnpm run dev
+```
+
+The UI runs on port 5000 at `0.0.0.0` with all hosts allowed for Replit preview compatibility.
+
+## Configuration
+
+- Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in required values
+- The gateway requires at minimum: `OPENCLAW_GATEWAY_TOKEN` and at least one AI provider API key
+- Channel tokens (Telegram, Discord, etc.) are set per-channel
+
+## Key Files
+
+- `src/` — Main backend TypeScript source
+- `ui/` — Frontend control dashboard (Lit + Vite)
+- `extensions/` — Channel integration plugins
+- `packages/` — Shared sub-packages
+- `.env.example` — Environment variable template
+- `docker-compose.yml` — Docker setup for self-hosting
+
+## Notes
+
+- The `packageManager` field in `package.json` was updated from `pnpm@10.23.0` to `pnpm@10.26.1` to match the Replit environment
+- Vite server config updated to use port 5000 and `allowedHosts: true` for Replit proxy compatibility
